{{!-- The featured post and the security feed, side by side.

     Why one partial that branches on the setting, instead of putting the grid in
     collection-layout.hbs: the hero must stay *exactly* where it is, full width, when
     no feed is configured — which is the default for every site that has not set
     `sec_feed_api_url`. A grid that is always present would reserve a 1/3 column for
     an absent widget and shrink the hero, and it would change the HTML of every
     collection page for no visible reason. So the grid exists only when the feed does.

     The duplicate `{{#match}}` below is the cost of that: a Handlebars partial cannot
     take an argument conditionally, and the alternative — always emitting the grid —
     costs every site a layout change it did not ask for. One line, one reason.

     The featured post owns the row's height, and the feed is stretched to it. The
     class this replaces, `items-start`, did the opposite: each column sat at the top
     of the row at its own height, so the 1/3 column was content-sized, and `{{> "sec-feed"}}`
     grew it or shrank it with every poll. That is the "island of variable height" this
     layout used to have.

     Two mechanisms, and both are needed. Grid's default `align-items: stretch` gives
     the columns the row's height rather than their own, and taking the feed panel out
     of the row's intrinsic sizing (below) is what stops the larger column from deciding
     that height. `items-start` defeated the first, and an in-flow grid item defeats the
     second on its own.

     Why not a fixed row height, or `h-full` on an in-flow column: the hero's
     max-content height is not a constant. It is 552.5px at 1024x900 (the 16:9 image box
     is taller there than the text beside it) and 515px at 1280 and above, and it is
     467px of hero card plus the card's `mb-12`. So any declared height is wrong at one
     end, and `height: 100%` cannot help either: an auto-sized grid track is indefinite,
     a percentage against an indefinite height resolves to `auto`, and the panel would
     size to its content and grow the track it was measuring against. See
     docs/adr/0003-security-feed-widget.md.

     `locale` only selects which hero partial renders; the feed gets its own strings from
     the page language. --}}
{{#if @custom.sec_feed_api_url}}
<div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-3">
    {{!-- 2/3: the featured post. --}}
    <div class="lg:col-span-2">
        {{#match locale "=" "es"}}{{> "featured-hero-es"}}{{else match locale "=" "br"}}{{> "featured-hero-br"}}{{else}}{{> "featured-hero"}}{{/match}}
    </div>

    {{!-- 1/3: the security feed, as a column beside the hero. Its bottom margin matches
         the featured card's, so both blocks leave the same space before the post grid;
         it stacks below the hero on mobile, where the hero stays first.

         On lg the panel is positioned rather than laid out in the column: the column is
         the containing block (`lg:relative`) and `partials/sec-feed.hbs` is pinned to it
         (`lg:absolute lg:inset-0`). That is not decoration, it is what makes the hero own
         the row height. An in-flow grid item contributes its content height to an
         auto-sized row track, so a feed of twenty advisories would size the track no
         matter how the column was clamped, because `min-h-0` bounds a flex item, not a grid
         track, which is why the earlier `h-full min-h-0` column still measured 752.5
         instead of the hero's 515. Out of flow, the feed contributes nothing, the track
         is the hero's max-content height, and the panel is then stretched back onto the
         column it was taken out of. Below lg nothing is positioned, so the stack is the
         plain one: hero first, gap-8, feed under it.

         `mb-12` is the featured card's own bottom margin, repeated here. It does two
         things and both are visible at a glance: on lg the panel is pinned to this
         column's padding box, so the margin shortens the panel to the *card's* height
         (515 minus 48 is the card's 467) and its bottom edge lines up with the card's;
         on every width the margin is the space the row needs before the post grid, which
         an un-margined panel would otherwise sit flush against. Change it here only
         together with the `mb-12` on the hero card in partials/featured-hero*.hbs, or
         the two columns stop matching. --}}
    <div class="lg:col-span-1 lg:relative lg:min-h-0 mb-12">
        {{> "sec-feed" locale=locale}}
    </div>
</div>
{{else}}
{{#match locale "=" "es"}}{{> "featured-hero-es"}}{{else match locale "=" "br"}}{{> "featured-hero-br"}}{{else}}{{> "featured-hero"}}{{/match}}
{{/if}}
